A conversion provider whose source is not convertible to its target would emit
uncompilable Go. On this tolerated-invalid input (a Config value is not convertible to
*Config) plumb reports a located diagnostic instead of silently emitting (*Config)(x).
On valid input the blank-var assignment type-checks, so the source is always convertible.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrInvalidConversion
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Config struct{}

//plumb:build
var _ *Config = Config{}
